            <ArticleTitle>Usefulness of transthoracic echocardiography for identification of left atrial thrombus before balloon mitral valvuloplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1132-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The objectives of this study were (1) to identify clinical and transthoracic echocardiographic features of patients with mitral stenosis who have thrombus recognized on transesophageal echocardiography, and (2) to define a clinical and echocardiographic model to predict the presence of left atrial thrombus in these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
